              <Accordion class="faq-1 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">1. How much does a business website cost in 2026?</Fragment>
                <p>
                  Business website costs depend on the number of pages, design requirements,
                  functionality, content needs and integrations. A straightforward informational
                  website generally costs less than a custom website with e-commerce, booking
                  systems or complex integrations. I provide project-specific quotations based on
                  your requirements, so you can understand the scope and investment before
                  development begins.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-2 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">
                  2. How long does it take to build a business website?
                </Fragment>
                <p>
                  The timeline depends on the project's size and complexity. A small website may
                  take a few weeks, while larger websites involving custom features, e-commerce or
                  integrations can require more time. The schedule also depends on content
                  readiness, feedback and revisions. I establish a realistic timeline after
                  reviewing the project requirements.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-3 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">
                  3. What is the best website platform for a small business?
                </Fragment>
                <p>
                  There isn't one platform that suits every business. WordPress is a flexible choice
                  for content-rich and service-based websites, Shopify is designed for e-commerce,
                  and platforms such as Wix Studio may suit other requirements. I recommend a
                  platform based on your goals, budget, content management needs and long-term
                  plans.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-4 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">4. What should a small business website include?</Fragment>
                <p>
                  A professional small business website should clearly explain its services,
                  establish trust and make contacting the business easy. Essential features often
                  include responsive design, intuitive navigation, service information, clear calls
                  to action, contact details, fast loading pages and basic SEO foundations.
                  Additional functionality depends on the business.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-5 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">5. How do I know if my website needs a redesign?</Fragment>
                <p>
                  Consider a redesign if your website is difficult to navigate, performs poorly on
                  mobile, looks outdated, loads slowly or no longer reflects your services. Low
                  enquiry rates and confusing user journeys can also indicate problems. Before
                  recommending a complete redesign, I assess whether targeted improvements could
                  address the issues.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-6 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">
                  6. Do I still need a website if my business uses social media?
                </Fragment>
                <p>
                  Social media can help businesses reach audiences, but a dedicated website gives
                  you more control over your content, branding and customer experience. Your website
                  can present detailed service information, support search visibility, collect
                  enquiries and connect customers with your business without relying entirely on a
                  social platform.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
              <Accordion class="faq-7 accordion is-closed block flex-block">
                <Fragment slot="title">
                  7. Can a website actually help a business generate more enquiries?
                </Fragment>
                <p>
                  Yes, a well-planned website can create more opportunities for enquiries by
                  explaining your offer clearly, attracting relevant visitors and making it easier
                  to contact you. Effective calls to action, helpful content, strong mobile
                  usability and a streamlined enquiry process can improve the experience. Results
                  depend on traffic quality, competition, your offer and ongoing optimization.
                </p>
              </Accordion>
